## Deploy with Asset Bundles

Prerequisites:

- Databricks workspace with <Apps / Genie space / SQL warehouse / ...> as needed
- A **Lakebase** project/branch/database (with any required extension, e.g. pgvector)
- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/install.html) logged
  into the target workspace

Steps:

1. **Set variables** — override any workspace-specific value, especially the
   Lakebase database path:

   ```bash
   databricks bundle deploy -t demo \
     --var lakebase_database="projects/<project>/branches/<branch>/databases/<id>"
   ```

2. **(Any once-per-workspace setup)** — e.g. granting the app service principal
   access to the Lakebase project, creating a Postgres role, etc.

3. **Run / open** the deployed resource and confirm it works.

